DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       The  ppaammwwiippeeoouutt  utility takes a Netpbm image as input and the uses two
       opposite edges of the image to wipe out anything in between.   You  can
       use  it in combination with ppaammccuutt and ppnnmmppaassttee / ppaammccoommpp to remove un‐
       wanted parts of a larger image.  The program replaces the pixels in be‐
       tween the two edges with a gradient from one edge to the other.

       In  ttoopp--bboottttoomm  mode, the program reads the whole image into memory be‐
       fore it can start processing.  In lleefftt--rriigghhtt it will read the  image  a
       row  at  the  time,  process  that row and write it to the output file.
       Therefore, in case of very large images, it may be better  to  use  in‐
       stead  of  "ppaammwwiippeeoouutt  --ttbb"  a pipe of "ppaammfflliipp --ccww || ppaammwwiippeeoouutt --llrr ||
       ppaammfflliipp --ccccww".

       In his blog at

       www.i-am.ws ⟨http://www.i-am.ws/entry/pnmblend_disappearing_act⟩ ,  the
       author wrote about a predecessor of "pamwipeout" at the time named "pn‐
       mblend". It shows a good example of what can be accomplished with  this
       utility.


